stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR

    [*] --> pending: Scheduled, social, or continuation admission

    pending --> running: Due job claimed<br/>lease version incremented
    retry_wait --> running: Retry becomes due<br/>job claimed again
    running --> running: Lease renewed
    running --> running: Expired lease reclaimed<br/>lease version incremented

    running --> succeeded: Validated output published atomically
    running --> retry_wait: Retryable provider or output failure<br/>future availability retained
    running --> skipped: Model skip, unsafe/repeated output,<br/>policy/context denial, or expiry
    running --> cancelled: Source removed or execution cancelled
    running --> failed: Fatal provider/config/accounting failure,<br/>attempt exhaustion, or unavailable output

    pending --> skipped: Job expires before claim
    retry_wait --> skipped: Job expires before retry
    pending --> cancelled: Social source removed
    retry_wait --> cancelled: Social source removed
    running --> skipped: Source cleanup after immutable expiry

    failed --> retry_wait: Eligible trusted operator retry

    succeeded --> [*]
    skipped --> [*]
    cancelled --> [*]
    failed --> [*]: No eligible operator retry

    note right of pending
        Pending work has never been leased.
        Identity, source, expiry, persona,
        and chain limits are durable.
    end note

    note right of running
        Only the current lease version may
        reserve spend, settle, or publish.
        Provider calls run outside transactions.
    end note

    note right of retry_wait
        Retry timing is persisted.
        The worker never sleeps inside a pass
        waiting for one job's backoff.
    end note

    note right of succeeded
        Publication, provenance, job success,
        and continuation admission commit
        in one transaction.
    end note

    note right of failed
        Failed is terminal by default.
        Only an eligible admin retry may
        return it to retry_wait.
    end note
